WEBVTT

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.230
Say, Coconuts...

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:10.350
You may not have noticed
since you're so dense,

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:12.950
so I'm just gonna be bold and spit it out.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:17.200
Why...

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.530
"Ice"

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:18.530
...is your shop...

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.080
...so...

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:24.120
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.080
...run down like this?

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:26.460
It's been...

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.590
...three months since then.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.130
You think so?

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.720
Yeah! It's totally run down!

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:39.220
B-But we're somehow doing okay,
so don't worry! See ya!

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.980
Ah, hey! Somehow? Seriously?

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.200
Are they really doing okay?

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:49.270
I'm home!

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.360
This shop is done for.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:55.080
Oh, welcome back.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:58.200
"Done for"...?

00:00:58.990 --> 00:00:59.990
What?

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.250
Ah, well...

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:06.750
It's just like I said.

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:10.250
Are you okay?

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:15.050
Your eyes are even more dead than usual...

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:50.270
To put it bluntly, it's like our
shop is in financial trouble.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:54.390
Since we don't have any customers,
our sales keep falling.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:59.610
That makes it hard to keep up
with repairs around the shop.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.990
And Kokonotsu isn't listening...

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:06.290
Yeah... The truth is, I already knew...

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.200
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:09.200
...what Dad was telling me.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.540
But for some reason,

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:14.540
I thought that things would
eventually work out if I stayed here.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.880
Kokonotsu?

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.130
Hello?

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.180
I was waiting for it...

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.020
I was just... waiting...

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.510
You hold onto this...

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.190
Y-You can't!

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:36.820
You can't go out of business, Dad!

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:37.940
I-It's not like I want to.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.440
I have a winning bar!

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:43.280
A winner can only be exchanged
at the dagashi shop you bought it!

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:50.750
Kokonotsu... I like that look
of determination on your face.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:57.210
Oh, I see! This is about Hotaru, huh?

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:05.300
You sometimes take the winning Homerun Bar
stick out of the drawer and stare at it.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.720
"Meito Homerun! (Won 1 free bar)"

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.430
So it's Hotaru's, huh?

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:08.560
Wha...?!

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.180
You're lucky it's just me who saw that.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.440
If someone else sees that, they'd likely
get pretty creeped out, so be careful.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:19.030
I told you not to peek in my room, didn't I?!

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:21.870
Shall we do it, Kokonotsu?

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:22.820
Huh?

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:27.700
We'll revive... our dagashi shop!

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.310
Dad...! Yeah!

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.210
Well then, first... we'll clean the shop!

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.290
Yeah!

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:38.790
Then let's see who gets outside first!

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.000
--Come on, Dad!

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.670
--Hey!
--Come on, Dad!

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.630
Don't run inside the shop!

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:56.520
Whaaaat?!

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.820
And thus, Dad ended up in the hospital.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.980
Estimated recovery time... one month.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:07.240
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.610
You can handle this!

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:09.990
In any case, hang in there while I'm gone.

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:11.040
Yeah...

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.790
Manager Kokonotsu... for now.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:18.000
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.750
How shabby...

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:22.550
Right, it's not that I wasn't aware of it.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:28.680
That's how much I was weighed down...
by Hotaru's disappearance.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.010
Why...?

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:38.020
I'm definitely worried about Coconuts.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:41.400
He's always had those scary dead eyes,

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.780
but they're even more like
a deep-sea fish's lately.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.280
What a terrible thing to say...

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:48.030
But well, you may be right.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:51.280
Right? We should do 
something to cheer him up.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:54.200
Ah, but don't talk about Hotaru, okay?

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.540
As soon as he hears her name,
he may roll his eyes back.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:59.290
What? That sounds funn-- Hm?

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:00.670
Oh?

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:04.920
I'm cleaning right now, so it's messy inside,
but you're welcome to come in.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.430
Hey, he seems fine.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.850
I'm sorry. Sounds like I worried you, huh?

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:13.600
You did, seriously...

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.930
On top of that, I'm having 
you help me clean...

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.980
Don't worry about it. Ever since Hotaru
disappeared, you were like a dea--

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:23.400
Hey, brother!

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.980
Ah, well...

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.400
But I'm okay now.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:30.030
I'm sure Hotaru will come again.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:33.910
So I'm gonna turn this shop back into
a place where people would gather.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:35.950
Coconuts...

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.370
Also, if we don't get customers soon,

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.630
the only food I'll have to eat
is the dagashi in the shop.

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:44.290
Why did you wait until it got to that point?

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:52.180
Well then, I'll go ditch the trash.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.510
Thanks!

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:58.890
Let's see... After Umai-bou is...

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:00.690
Coconuts, what was it?

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:02.860
Get a Move On, You Cod!

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:07.440
Where the heck did that come from?

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.410
Was I being slow?

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.660
No, I wasn't... right...?

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:18.250
And so what if I was slow?
He does realize I'm helping him out, right?

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.870
And he even called me a cod...?
What's his damage?!

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:25.200
So... did you get it, Sa--

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:28.840
Yikes! What? What is it?!

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:31.840
"Get a Move On, You Cod!"
"Exotic Flavor"
"Super Hot"

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.840
"Get a Move On, You Cod!"...

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:36.850
Its name includes a pun on the word "cod."
It can be served as a side dish as well.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:39.770
Sorry.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:40.600
Do you wanna try it?

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.650
Adults like to snack on it while drinking.

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:45.150
I also heard that it's good
to put it in soup and stuff.

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:46.110
"Get a Move On, You Cod!"
"Exotic Flavor"
"Super Hot"

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:50.990
You're right! It tastes good!

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:51.860
But...

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:54.870
"Get a Move On, You Cod!"
"Exotic Flavor"
"Super Hot"

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.230
...its name and illustration, too...

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.620
And this thing written on the back.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:02.620
"We made it hot with exotic flavor! Let's have
a bite and shout 'Get a move on, you cod!'"

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:02.620
"Let's have a bite and shout,
'Get a move on, you cod!'"

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:05.580
Is this... something we should do?

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:06.750
What?! Are we doing it?

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:09.760
No way! Who'd do that, right?!
It's embarrassing!

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.970
At a time like this, if it were Hotaru...

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:22.980
I wonder why Hotaru suddenly disappeared.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.350
I wonder if Coconuts 
knows something about it.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.690
It's been a while since 
we spent time like this.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:31.240
What?

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:33.790
Talking about dagashi, I mean.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.300
I've been acting down for a long time.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:41.250
You've been trying to cheer me up, and yet...

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.160
Thank you.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.000
I didn't do anything.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:52.500
But you helped me quite a bit. Now, too.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.810
It's kind of embarrassing, isn't it?

00:08:57.590 --> 00:09:01.850
I'm so happy! I feel really embarrassed!

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.770
Hey, guys! I saw a cat earlier
on the street and it was--

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:06.270
B-Brother!

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.520
O-Oh, hey...

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:11.530
What's up with that reaction 
and this situation?

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.030
What? What're you talking about?

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:15.700
Well... Um... You know...

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.280
"Get a Move On, You Cod!"
"Exotic Flavor"
"Super Hot"

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.700
Y-You wanna "get your groove on, you cod!"

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:23.040
How about you "get a clue, you moron?!"

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.540
It's gotten a lot better.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.540
Yeah, this is pretty good!

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:31.840
Yeah!

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.390
No... I can't just keep everything the same.

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:40.040
I have to start something new.

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:44.270
What customers want...
What they'd like to have...

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:45.180
What's convenient...

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:48.690
I have to take a fresh look at those things.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:50.730
Whoa...

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:52.440
You sound kinda cool.

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:53.240
What?

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:59.950
Well, people at dagashi shops do think
about many things other than dagashi.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:03.700
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:03.700
From plastic models and toys to stationery...

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:08.710
...dagashi shops may be like the forerunner
of convenience stores, so to speak.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.460
Oh, I see! A convenience store!

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:13.960
Fortunately, there's no
convenience store around here!

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.980
In other words, if I take 
advantage of that...!

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.050
C-Coconuts...

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:20.770
Hm?

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.830
Um... Look over there.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:25.910
Hm?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:28.640
What?

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:32.480
"Opening Sale"

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:32.480
What...? What?!

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:35.780
W-We have a convenience store now!

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:37.990
"Ambulance, Get a Move On, You Cod!, and..."

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:16.510
"Next time:
Convenience Store, Job Magazine, and...'"

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.370
Next time: "Convenience Store,
Job Magazine, and..."

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:16.290
Coconuts, this is bad!
Your dagashi shop is in trouble!
